[Music]  surviving in venezuela has been a  challenge for maria jelitsa vergara  she received a kidney transplant 17  years ago  but last year her kidneys began to fail  again  and like thousands of other high-risk  patients in the country  she's hoping to get her second covid19  vaccine dose  soon it's been a week since i was  supposed to get my second dose  i have no clue what's going on i don't  know why they didn't do everything right  why can't they do it right for once the  same thing with transplants  four years without a transplant all  patients like me are in the hands of god  i need forty two dollars to pay for  medications and my pension is one dollar  and i need to have two jobs venezuela is  struggling with u.s sanctions  and an economic crisis that is impacting  its ability to fight against the disease  the south american nation is part of the  kovac system  which is a collaborative effort designed  to help countries like venezuela  get access to vaccines but that's proven  to be a challenge  so far it has only received around 3.5  million doses from china and russia  and the country is currently testing  thousands of doses of vaccines from cuba  two months ago kovacs announced payments  made to the system by venezuela had been  blocked by the swiss bank ubs  even though the biden administration  said all related covet purchases were  exempted from the sanctions  on sunday president nicolas maduro said  the kovac system has failed venezuela  we fulfilled our promises two months ago  we gave them all our money by doing  magic to liberate funds that were  blocked  the government of the united states then  unblocked more money for us  and that money is there in an account  and the kovacs has failed the people of  venezuela  either you give us the vaccines or  return our money  earlier this year venezuela rejected  around 2 million astrazeneca vaccines  from kovacs  due to safety concerns but opposition  figures say  venezuela could be accessing vaccines  for free  miguel pizarro who is currently on exile  say  the reasons why we don't have access to  free vaccines like countries like syria  sudan or yemen countries that have  humanitarian emergencies that are  acknowledged by the united nations  the reason is the obscurity of  statistics of numbers  in front of the world bank are numbers  that show when venezuela enjoyed an oil  bonanza  and that's not the case anymore  as politicians baker over who is to  blame for the hardships in the country  millions of venezuelans are impatiently  waiting for an opportunity to get the  vaccine  people like maria jeriza vergara  struggling with a life-threatening  disease says  it's her only chance of surviving covet  19.  terisa

